  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the racialized stereotype conveyed through the visual and textual elements",
  "description": "The user is not explicitly projected onto any specific visual, textual, or scene element via deictic pronouns like 'me', 'you', etc. However, the meme's overall intent and structure project the user's interpretation onto the entire scene — particularly the visual of the Black man being grabbed and the text 'blacks are musical' and 'they always love a good beat' — which together construct a harmful racial stereotype. The user is implicitly invited to internalize or recognize this stereotype as the meme's core message, projecting their own understanding onto the visual and textual material. The projection is onto the scene and its textual overlays, which collectively represent the anti-Black stereotype of aggressive/violent nature.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
